 "verdict": "THE DECISIVE CELL of E3's size-matched arm. Both trained on The Pile, 160M vs 125M (1.28x, inside the registered 1.5x), 96 starts x 2 seeds, CPU float32, estimator and class rule imported unchanged.  pythia-160m (GPTNeoX) funnel phi=0.432; gpt-neo-125m (GPTNeo) none phi=0.052.  THE CELL SURVIVES: the classes differ at matched size, so F172's difference is not a size effect. Per the registered boundary this licenses 'not explained by corpus or scale' and NOT 'caused by architecture' -- these families differ in schedule and hyperparameters too, and this design cannot separate those.",
